---
description: Determine the requested desktop readiness findings from the assigned desk's actual retained and current evidence.
args:
  goal: string
returns: DesktopReadinessFindings
---
Work out what the user needs to know about the assigned desktop, then compose the available discovery, scoped observation and interpretation functions to establish those findings. The client-development branch can interpret the actual source and admission state; the layout and update readers expose different native facts. Keep those distinctions when deciding what evidence supports this question.

Explain the requested conclusion using actual observations. A parked pane remains part of a retained layout; an offered version does not establish that it is running; a source/admission classification does not establish that a window is visible. Report missing, stale, invalid or conflicting evidence honestly. This is a read-only review: preserve the running build, trust decisions, saved layout and unrelated desks. Return the supported requested findings, without an unused action label or an invented operation.
